**Proposed code-level fixes (based on source analysis):**

**1. `src/util/queue.ts` — Add capacity limit:**
```typescript
// Current: unbounded queue — items never dropped
push(item: T) {
  const resolve = this.resolvers.shift()
  if (resolve) resolve(item)
  else this.queue.push(item)  // ← no limit
}

// Proposed: cap queue size, signal overflow to caller
private readonly limit: number
constructor(limit = 10000) { this.limit = limit }

push(item: T): boolean {
  const resolve = this.resolvers.shift()
  if (resolve) { resolve(item); return true }
  if (this.queue.length >= this.limit) return false  // drop or signal
  this.queue.push(item)
  return true
}
```

**2. `src/server/instance/event.ts:46-53` — Add idle timeout alongside heartbeat:**
```typescript
// Current: heartbeat pushes every 10s forever, even if consumer is dead
const heartbeat = setInterval(() => { q.push(...) }, 10_000)

// Proposed: also check if queue is draining
let lastConsumed = Date.now()
const heartbeat = setInterval(() => {
  if (Date.now() - lastConsumed > 60_000) { stop(); return }  // idle 60s → kill
  q.push(...)
}, 10_000)
// Update lastConsumed in the for-await loop after each successful writeSSE
```

**3. `src/server/instance/event.ts:71` — Don't rely solely on `onAbort`:**
```typescript
// Current: cleanup ONLY via onAbort — never fires on CLOSE_WAIT
stream.onAbort(stop)

// Proposed: also wrap writeSSE in try/catch — socket error triggers cleanup
try {
  for await (const data of q) {
    if (data === null) return
    try {
      await stream.writeSSE({ data })
      lastConsumed = Date.now()
    } catch {
      stop(); return  // write failed → socket dead → clean up
    }
  }
} finally { stop() }
```

**4. `src/lsp/client.ts:52` — Prune diagnostics for closed files:**
```typescript
// Current: Map grows forever, only entries replaced on re-open
const diagnostics = new Map<string, Diagnostic[]>()

// Proposed: clear entries for files not in `files` map (closed files)
// or add a periodic prune of entries older than N minutes
```

**5. `src/mcp/index.ts` — Kill previous MCP processes before spawning new ones:**
The 7-10× duplicate process sets suggest that `closeClient()` (line 548) is not being called when instances are re-initialized. Check that instance disposal properly closes all MCP clients before new ones are created.
